[38;5;246m [3G⎿[5G [39mCreated[14G[1minbox/04-scanner-platform-v2.md[46G[22m[38;5;246m(+48[51G-0)[39m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  1 +[38;5;231mFrom: Priya Natarajan <priya.natarajan@northwick.example> (Scanner Platform, team lead)                             [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  2 +[38;5;231mTo: finding-relay owner <sec-platform@northwick.example>                                                            [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  3 +[38;5;231mCc: Ravi Menon <ravi.menon@northwick.example>                                                                       [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  4 +[38;5;231mDate: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:20 +0000                                                                                  [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  5 +[38;5;231mSubject: findings contract v2: dual-publish from 2 Nov, v1 stops 16 Nov                                             [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  6 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                                    [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  7 +[38;5;231mHi,                                                                                                                 [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  8 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                                    [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  9 +[38;5;231mRavi tells me the relay has a new owner from Monday, so this goes to you                                            [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 10 +[38;5;231mrather than to Dana. Version 2 of the findings contract is ready and we would                                       [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 11 +[38;5;231mlike to start publishing it in two weeks. Draft contract and a preview sample                                       [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 12 +[38;5;231mare attached (Ravi put them in your repository as                                                                   [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 13 +[38;5;231m`contracts/findings.v2.asyncapi.yaml` and                                                                           [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 14 +[38;5;231m`dev/samples/findings.v2-preview.ndjson`).                                                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 15 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                                    [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 16 +[38;5;231mWhat changes:                                                                                                       [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 17 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                                    [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 18 +[38;5;231m1. `schema_version: 2` on every message.                                                                            [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 19 +[38;5;231m2. `severity` becomes an integer 0–4 (info 0, low 1, medium 2, high 3,                                              [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 20 +[38;5;231m   critical 4). Too many consumers were string-matching it.                                                         [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 21 +[38;5;231m3. `evidence.match` and `evidence.context` are gone. In their place                                                 [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 22 +[38;5;231m   `evidence.match_ref` is a URL into the evidence vault                                                            [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 23 +[38;5;231m   (`https://evidence.northwick.example/v1/findings/<id>/match`), readable                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 24 +[38;5;231m   with the scanner-platform read role, kept for 30 days. The raw match was                                         [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 25 +[38;5;231m   leaving our pipeline in too many places.                                                                         [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 26 +[38;5;231m4. `fingerprint` is now sha256 (64 hex) over                                                                        [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 27 +[38;5;231m   `scanner|rule|repo|path|sha256(match)`. The v1 sha1 was over the raw                                             [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 28 +[38;5;231m   match, which pushed secret-shaped text through our hashing pipeline and                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 29 +[38;5;231m   Legal wants it gone. We know what this means for you: the same finding                                           [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 30 +[38;5;231m   has a different fingerprint in v2 than in v1. The preview sample is the                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 31 +[38;5;231m   first 20 findings of the v1 export you have under `dev/samples/`,                                                [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 32 +[38;5;231m   re-emitted in v2 shape with new ids, so you can diff them line by line.                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 33 +[38;5;231m5. Subjects are `findings.v2.<scanner>`. We publish into the same `FINDINGS`                                        [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 34 +[38;5;231m   stream; your `findings.>` filter will pick them up without a change on                                           [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 35 +[38;5;231m   your side.                                                                                                       [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 36 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                                    [39m[49m
