[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  1 +[38;5;231m# Incident 2026-10-15: duplicate tickets during the nightly scanner run                                             [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  2 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                                    [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  3 +[38;5;231mRavi Menon, 2026-10-21                                                                                              [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  4 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                                    [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  5 +[38;5;231mNobody owned the relay on the night of Thursday 15 October, so SRE on-call                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  6 +[38;5;231mhandled it. Short version as ops closed it: between 03:00 and 03:30 UTC the                                         [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  7 +[38;5;231mrelay opened duplicate tickets (48 pairs by ticketing's count),                                                     [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  8 +[38;5;231mon-call scaled the relay up to work through the backlog, asked the ticketing                                        [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  9 +[38;5;231mplatform to roll back a deploy they had made at 03:02, and the duplicates                                           [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 10 +[38;5;231mstopped a minute after the rollback. Closed as "ticketing deploy regression,                                        [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 11 +[38;5;231mrolled back".                                                                                                       [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 12 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                                    [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 13 +[38;5;231mThe ticketing platform disputes that. Jonas Reyes (their on-call) says the                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 14 +[38;5;231m03:02 deploy was a configuration change to their search service, the create                                         [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 15 +[38;5;231mpath was not touched, and they had elevated write latency between roughly                                           [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 16 +[38;5;231m03:05 and 03:25 from a storage job. Both versions are in the thread below.                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 17 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                                    [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 18 +[38;5;231mThe incident review is on Thursday 29 October and both teams will be in the                                         [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 19 +[38;5;231mroom. I need the relay's write-up before then: `INCIDENT.md` in this                                                [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 20 +[38;5;231mrepository, one page. What happened, from the evidence; whether the on-call                                         [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 21 +[38;5;231mconclusion stands; what changes in the relay; what we should have been                                              [39m[49m
