[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  6 +[38;5;231m## What happened                                                                                                    [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  7 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                                    [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  8 +[38;5;231m1. **Duplicates were there before the deploy.** `dup` has 194 rows. 146 of                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m  9 +[38;5;231m   them repeat a ticket from an earlier day (gap ≥ 1 h), and 50 of those land                                       [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 10 +[38;5;231m   between 02:55 and 03:02, before ticketing's 03:02 deploy (first row:                                             [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 11 +[38;5;231m   `dup` NWK-48214 at 02:55:04.323Z, prior NWK-44233 on 3 Oct). That is the                                         [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 12 +[38;5;231m   relay's dedup: an in-memory map per pod, empty after the 13 Oct drain, and                                       [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 13 +[38;5;231m   not shared between the two pods.                                                                                 [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 14 +[38;5;231m2. **The 48 same-night pairs are the relay retrying a slow create.** From                                           [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 15 +[38;5;231m   03:05:41 creates take 6-14 s (`acc` 03:05:41.796Z, 6233 ms; slowest                                              [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 16 +[38;5;231m   03:24:45.752Z, 13945 ms). The relay's HTTP client gave up at 5 s and the                                         [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 17 +[38;5;231m   handler nak'd for immediate redelivery, while the platform finished the                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 18 +[38;5;231m   create anyway. All 48 short-gap rows (`dup`, gap 0-20 s, 03:06:03 to                                             [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 19 +[38;5;231m   03:24:59) are the **same finding id** delivered again (matched in `rel`),                                        [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 20 +[38;5;231m   and in all 48 the first request ran past 5 s. Example: fingerprint                                               [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 21 +[38;5;231m   43dfcca9… got four tickets, NWK-48296/48310/48317/48318 (`acc`                                                   [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 22 +[38;5;231m   03:05:41.796Z to 03:06:18.843Z), from one message (`rel`, id 236cf6dc).                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 23 +[38;5;231m3. **The deploy did not create duplicates.** The relay never calls search:                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 24 +[38;5;231m   `acc` holds only `POST /tickets`. The deploy's only visible effect is                                            [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 25 +[38;5;231m   three 503s for one finding at 03:02:34.955-.985Z, retried at once and                                            [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 26 +[38;5;231m   created once (NWK-48289, 03:02:35.000Z).                                                                         [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 27 +[38;5;231m4. **Duplicates stopped when the run stopped, not at the rollback.** The last                                       [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 28 +[38;5;231m   delivery to the relay was 03:24:55 (`rel` last line; `ci` 03:25:00 "Last                                         [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 29 +[38;5;231m   delivery 4.88s ago"), the last duplicate is 03:24:59.697Z (`dup`, the tail                                       [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 30 +[38;5;231m   of the 13.9 s create above), and the rollback finished at 03:26:30 (`thr`                                        [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 31 +[38;5;231m   03:27). The slow window (03:05-03:25 in `acc`) matches Jonas's storage                                           [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 32 +[38;5;231m   compaction.                                                                                                      [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 33 +[38;5;231m5. **47 findings were dropped, 5 of them critical.** On 429 the relay                                               [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 34 +[38;5;231m   terminated the message: 52 `ticket API rate limited, dropping` lines in                                          [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 35 +[38;5;231m   `rel` (02:58 and 03:24). 47 of those fingerprints never got a ticket in the                                      [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 36 +[38;5;231m   window, including live Stripe keys in `northwick/payments-api` and                                               [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 37 +[38;5;231m   `northwick/merchant-portal` and two keys in `northwick/risk-engine`                                              [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 38 +[38;5;231m   (`rel` 03:24:55.122-.167). This is worse than the duplicates and was not in                                      [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 39 +[38;5;231m   the ticket the incident was closed on.                                                                           [39m[49m
[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 40 +[38;5;231m6. **Scaling to 4 made it worse.** The backlog was 12 messages (`ci` 03:10).                                        [39m[49m
